# Invariant Aware Programming

Ryan Berger
Software Corectness Enthusiast
https://ryanberger.me

## The Invariant

A property about a program that doesn't change

.play division.go /START OMIT/,/END OMIT/

## Problems They Solve

- Commenting code and documentation
- Preventing data corruption
- Proof by code
- Debugging (asserts)
- Performance

## Enforcement

- Control flow
> ```
> if condition {
>     return thing
> }
> // !condition must hold
> ```

- Number Theory
> `abs()`, `%`, two's complement etc. 

- Synchronization
> ```
> mu.Lock()
> counter++
> mu.Unlock()

## Being Invariant Aware

- Understanding the set of all inputs and outputs
- Understanding _how_ to restrict the problem space
- Finding tradeoffs associated with lazy/eager enforcement

